    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature creation from window partitioning, and the window step keeps the tokens rather than discarding them.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field. That field is the carrier that preserves spatial information for the thought process. The window operator partitions the field into tokens, so the tokens are carried forward rather than collapsed away.",
