    {
      "id": "s03-params",
      "intent": "DQ-CTM-SR is compact relative to CARN but not the cheapest method; among these five methods, its parameter count is second largest.",
      "claim": "Table 1 reports Params for CARN 1.592M, IMDN 0.715M, RFDN 0.550M, CATANet 0.535M, and DQ-CTM-SR 1.129M.",
      "narration": "The smallest models in this comparison are CATANet and RFDN, both just over half a million parameters. DQ-CTM-SR has one point one two nine million parameters, making it the second largest of the five. The table supports a measured claim: ThinkSR is competitive with CNN baselines, but parameter count is not its cheapest result.",
      "evidence": [
